  • A single-use peristaltic arrangement assumed suitable for 100 L/min and 6 bar without documented tubing pressure, fatigue-life, extractables, and flow-capability evidence.

Preliminary specification
────────────────────────────────────────
  • Service: Chromatography skid feed and product transfer
  • Operating flow: 20–100 L/min with minimum, normal, and maximum recipe points defined before RFQ
  • Differential pressure: 3–6 bar operating; maximum allowable and shutoff cases to be coordinated with column and skid design pressure
  • Fluid: Protein solution, 1–5 cP; density, vapor pressure, composition, solids, gas content, and shear acceptance criteria to be supplied
  • Wetted metal: 316L stainless steel with material certification appropriate to the project
  • Elastomers: EPDM as DIR basis, subject to product, CIP chemical, hot-water, extractables, and temperature compatibility review
  • Internal finish: Hygienic finish and electropolishing requirements to be defined by the project and vendor capability
  • Connections: Hygienic clamp or project-standard sanitary connections, sized to limit suction loss and support complete drainage
  • Cleaning: Automated CIP and hot-water sanitization; vendor to state allowable temperature, concentration, pressure, and exposure duration
  • Sterilization: SIP is not required by the DIR and shall not be claimed unless separately specified and demonstrated
  • Drainability: Pump casing, seal cavity, fittings, instruments, and connected tubing to drain in installed orientation
  • Seal: Hygienic mechanical seal suitable for protein service, CIP, hot-water cycling, and anticipated dry-run risk; single versus flushed arrangement to be reviewed
  • Drive: Washdown-suitable motor and VFD with hygienic skid installation and adequate low-speed cooling
  • Flow control: Closed-loop control from a hygienic flowmeter; recipe ramp rates and acceptable accuracy to be defined
  • Pressure instrumentation: Sanitary suction and discharge pressure measurement, with column-inlet pressure monitored where hydraulically distinct
  • Protection: Low suction pressure, low flow, high discharge pressure, high-high column pressure, motor overload, and dry-run logic
  • NPSH: Calculate NPSHa at worst case and select only where the project-approved margin over vendor NPSHr is maintained
  • Operating envelope: Vendor curve to show startup, minimum flow, normal flow, maximum flow, CIP, hot-water, and maximum resistance cases
  • Temperature rise: Vendor to identify low-flow operating restrictions; product recycle duration and allowable temperature increase to be project-defined
  • Documentation: Wetted materials, elastomer certificates, surface-finish evidence, performance curves, recommended maintenance, and hygienic design documentation
  • Verification: Final pump selection requires comparison with the actual system resistance curve and confirmation by the pump and chromatography-skid suppliers

Manufacturers: Alfa Laval (LKH hygienic centrifugal family), Fristam (FP hygienic centrifugal family), GEA (Hilge hygienic centrifugal families), SPX FLOW (Waukesha Cherry-Burrell hygienic pump families), PSG
